# --- supersession notes (D0106 ruling 2; D0128) ------------------------------
# tests/laws/m1/test_l1_rel.py
#   RETIRED, ONE node: test_l1_5_mixing_semirings_is_refused_by_name.
#   Its line 244 builds `Rel(("a",), [({"a": 1}, (2, Why.zero))])` as incidental
#   filler, and D0110 (owner-authorised) makes an unwitnessed nonzero annotation
#   unconstructible. The file stays frozen and unedited; the node's claim — mixing
#   semirings is refused by name — is carried forward verbatim by L2.2 in
#   tests/laws/m2/test_l2_sources.py. The entry is in governance/laws.yaml, and M2
#   Session B moved it from `pending` to `superseded` in the same change that landed
#   D0110 — so conftest.py now marks it xfail(strict=True) and it must FAIL, which it
#   does. Every other law in that file is unaffected and stands.
#
#   (The Session A spelling of this note named `governance/superseded-laws.yaml`, a
#   file that has never existed; the registry has been `governance/laws.yaml`
#   throughout. Corrected here rather than left to mislead — D0135.)
#
# docs/specs/m3.md
#   SUPERSEDED FORWARD, FOUR SENTENCES, no node retired. The frozen file is retained
#   and unedited; docs/specs/m3-corrections.md carries the claims at their true
#   strength. §7's input triple names three inputs where a first tick has two and
#   hides a binary node's operand-order collision (RT-M3-03); §7's "pure function of
#   those inputs" omitted the module-level registry (RT-M3-01, narrowed by D0197);
#   §7's "replaying a stream hits traces" was ruled false by the owner (D0171 ruling
#   1) because `advance` consults the trace and by default writes none; and §10's
#   L3.15 row repeats that last claim verbatim, which is the D0049 shape and was
#   found only by attacking the correction rather than reading it (D0203).
#   NOT the laws.yaml machinery: prose has no node to retire, and D0161 holds that
#   running the node-retirement half against prose is a category error. Record: D0204.
#
# tests/laws/m3/ — ALL NINE LAW FILES
#   SUPERSEDED FORWARD, WHOLE FILES, no node retired. Every M3 file is retained, unedited,
#   and still runs; its claim is restated under tests/laws/m4/ by a file that binds the
#   frozen oracle FROM ITS BYTES by file location (tests/laws/m4/_frozen_bind.py) instead of
#   a bare import a decoy can claim first (RT-M1-01, RT-M2-01, RT-M3-04):
#     test_l3_delta.py        L3.1-L3.4    -> test_l4_delta_superseding.py        L4.14
#     test_l3_linear.py       L3.5         -> test_l4_linear_superseding.py       L4.15
#     test_l3_join.py         L3.6         -> test_l4_join_superseding.py         L4.16
#     test_l3_integrated.py   L3.7-L3.8    -> test_l4_integrated_superseding.py   L4.17
#     test_l3_convergence.py  L3.9-L3.10   -> test_l4_convergence_superseding.py  L4.18
#     test_l3_graph.py        L3.11-L3.12  -> test_l4_graph_superseding.py        L4.19
#     test_l3_door.py         L3.13-L3.14  -> test_l4_door_superseding.py         L4.20
#     test_l3_executor.py     L3.15        -> test_l4_executor_superseding.py     L4.21
#     test_l3_differential.py L3.16        -> test_l4_differential_superseding.py L4.22
#   Rows that shared one frozen check became one law (RT-M3-05's answer, D0224). L4.21
#   states L3.15 as docs/specs/m3-corrections.md corrects it and does not carry its untested
#   quarantine clause. L4 ids, not L3: the evidence plugin keys a run by law id alone.
#   NO governance/laws.yaml entry: the M3 nodes still pass, so a strict xfail would be red.
#   The poison fixtures keep naming the M3 files. m3 §11's kill criterion now reads on
#   L4.19. Record: D0225.
#
# tests/laws/m4/test_l4_modes.py
#   RETIRED, ONE node: test_l4_4_tannen_run_spend_is_the_one_spelling_that_can_call.
#   It spends through `tannen run` against a `--budget` of its own; owner ruling D0240 item (2)
#   clamps the CLI to the checked-in budget.yaml, so under the clamp it must fail. Its claim is
#   carried forward by L5.1 (tests/laws/m5/test_l5_clamp.py, docs/specs/m5.md §6). Recorded in
#   governance/laws.yaml under `pending` at m5-laws-freeze (D0258), because the clamp had not
#   landed and the node still passed; M5 Session B1 moved it to `superseded` in the same change
#   that landed the clamp (D0263) — so conftest.py now marks it xfail(strict=True) and it must
#   FAIL, which it does, by the clamp's own `SpendDenied` naming `--budget-override`. The file
#   stays frozen and unedited; every other node in it is unaffected and stands.
#
# tests/laws/m4/test_l4_doorway.py
#   SUPERSEDED FORWARD, WHOLE FILE, no node retired. L4.9's network set was a hand-written
#   literal and process creation was not scanned (RT-M4-02). L5.2
#   (tests/laws/m5/test_l5_doorway.py, docs/specs/m5.md §7) derives all three forbidden sets —
#   the network set from the socket primitives by static import closure, the process and clock
#   sets from governance/importlinter.toml's contracts — and holds itself to
#   scripts/check_doorway.py by a differential clause (D0260). L4.9 is retained, unedited, and
#   still runs: it is weaker, not false.
